      reveal_hand: 'Hands are naturally revealed through trick play.',
      award_pot: 'System action after final trick.',
      play_card: 'Player may follow suit or play trump when holding suit led; undertrump restrictions apply after a trump is played.',
      draw: 'No draw step occurs after the initial deal.',
      discard: 'Cards are played into tricks, not discarded.',
      pass: 'Every active player must contribute one card to each trick.',
      bid: 'One prediction per player in range 0-157, with dealer speaking last.',
      meld: 'Differenzler does not score separate meld declarations.',
      go_out: 'The hand ends only after all tricks are completed.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 9 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Minimize cumulative penalty by predicting your own card-point total as accurately as possible.',
      "Turn-flow example: Trump suit is set by the suit of the bottom card of the cut packet. Beginning with the player to dealer's right and continuing clockwise, each player predicts a card-point total from 0 to 157. Play then proceeds anticlockwise with the player to dealer's right leading first. Usual Swiss Jass trick rules apply, including trump ranking and point values. After all tricks, each player's penalty is the absolute difference between predicted and achieved card points.",
      "Scoring example: Each player's hand penalty is the absolute difference between predicted and achieved card points. Lower cumulative penalty is better. After an agreed equal-dealer session length, the player with the lowest cumulative penalty wins..",
